# FIXED DEFECT 097, 2026-09-25: writing one element of a fixed array inside a
# group record passed `check` and aborted at run time as a compiler bug.
#
# SYMPTOM: this program, `check` 0, ran to exit 134 with *panic: entered
# unreachable code — this is a compiler bug*, on Darwin arm64 and Linux x86-64,
# and its C carried `warning: variable 't7' set but not used`: the index and the
# value were computed and then nothing wrote them. Reading `n.a[0]` worked, and
# so did writing the whole record.
#
# CAUSE: a store whose place holds an index goes to `write_element` in
# `selfhost/emit/container.hero`, which knew a `[T]` and a map and read a
# `T[N]` as "not a container step". The failure came back to
# `selfhost/emit/inst.hero`, which spelled it `hero_unreachable()`.
#
# FIX: a fixed-array step writes the element where it lies, as a field step
# does, through `fixed_subscript`: the one spelling of the bound check, which
# the read of `n.a[i]` goes through too, so the two cannot disagree. The index
# here is a literal and in range, so the check refuses nothing; the computed
# index and the one past the end have cases of their own.

extern "fixedbugs-a-fixed-array-element-is-written-in-place.h"
    record Nums tag nums
        a: i64[4]
    function nums_sum(n: Nums) -> i64

function main()
    n: Nums @= Nums(a: [1, 2, 3, 4])
    n.a[0] @ 9
    print("sum: ", nums_sum(n: n))
